Q: What is your logo design service?
A: Our logo design service is a strategic and creative process where we understand your business from your perspective, explore meaningful visual ideas, develop multiple unique design directions, and refine them into a professional logo and visual identity.

Q: How much does your logo design service cost?
A: Our logo design package costs ₹20,000 + GST.

Q: What is included in your logo design package?
A: The process includes a detailed 40-question logo briefing, strategic mind mapping, hand-sketching and concept development, 3 selected logo directions, digital development, colour and black-and-white versions, typography development, brand identity development, mockups, and a professional presentation.

Q: What happens before you start designing my logo?
A: We begin by sending you a detailed logo briefing document containing around 40 questions covering your business, design preferences, style preferences, colour choices, and other relevant information. This helps us understand your business from your perspective before we begin the creative process.

Q: Why do you ask so many questions before designing a logo?
A: A logo should represent the business, not just look attractive. The detailed briefing helps us understand your business, your perspective, preferences, positioning, and expectations so that the creative direction is based on meaningful information.

Q: What does your 40-question logo briefing cover?
A: It covers basic business information, design preferences, preferred and disliked styles, colour choices, visual preferences, and other questions that help us understand your business and the kind of identity you are looking for.

Q: Do I need to know exactly what I want before ordering a logo?
A: No. You only need to provide honest information about your business and preferences through the briefing. We use that information as the foundation for the creative exploration.

Q: What happens after I complete the logo briefing?
A: We analyse the information and begin a creative exploration process using mind mapping to identify meaningful visual possibilities connected to your business.

Q: What is mind mapping in your logo design process?
A: We create a web of words and ideas related to your business. We look for words and concepts that can potentially be converted into visual forms while still having a meaningful connection with your business.

Q: Why do you use mind mapping for logo design?
A: Mind mapping helps us move beyond obvious symbols and explore deeper visual connections related to your business. This allows us to discover more unique and conceptually relevant logo ideas.

Q: Do you directly start designing the logo on a computer?
A: No. We first explore ideas through mind mapping and sketching. This allows us to develop and evaluate concepts before committing to digital artwork.

Q: Do you sketch the logo concepts by hand?
A: Yes. We start sketching unique ideas based on the directions discovered through the mind-mapping process.

Q: What are logo design directions?
A: A direction is a distinct conceptual approach for representing your business visually. One direction may be used on its own, or multiple ideas can be combined to create a stronger and more meaningful concept.

Q: How many creative directions do you explore?
A: We explore multiple possible directions during the conceptual stage and eventually develop the strongest 3 directions into final digital logo concepts.

Q: How do you decide which logo ideas are worth developing?
A: We evaluate the sketches based on their conceptual connection with the business, uniqueness, visual potential, simplicity, and ability to work as a professional identity.

Q: How many logo concepts do I finally receive?
A: We develop the top 3 selected logo sketches into 3 distinct digital logo directions.

Q: Are the 3 logo concepts completely different?
A: Yes. The objective is to present 3 different creative directions while keeping all of them relevant to the same business.

Q: Will the three concepts be based on the same idea?
A: Not necessarily. Each direction can explore a different visual or conceptual approach, while remaining connected to the business and the information provided in the briefing.

Q: What happens after you select the top 3 sketches?
A: We recreate the selected sketches digitally and develop each direction into a more refined logo concept.

Q: Do you create different versions of each logo concept?
A: Yes. During the digital development stage, we create colour, black-and-white, and line-drawing versions of the selected logo directions.

Q: Why do you create a black-and-white version of the logo?
A: A strong logo should remain recognizable and effective even when colour is not available. The black-and-white version helps evaluate the fundamental strength of the design.

Q: What is a line-drawing version of the logo?
A: It is a simplified line-based representation of the logo that helps us evaluate and demonstrate the underlying construction and visual form of the symbol.

Q: Do you only focus on the logo symbol?
A: No. After developing the logo concepts, we also work on typography so that the symbol and the brand name work together as a cohesive identity.

Q: Do you select the font separately for the logo?
A: Yes. Typography is considered as an important part of the identity and is developed after the core logo directions have been established.

Q: Why is typography important in logo design?
A: The typeface, letterforms, spacing, and relationship between the symbol and brand name significantly influence how the overall identity looks and communicates.

Q: Do you create a complete brand identity with the logo?
A: Yes. The logo design process develops into a complete brand identity presentation, rather than stopping at a standalone symbol.

Q: What do you mean by complete brand identity?
A: It means developing the logo, typography, colour treatment, and overall visual relationship into a cohesive identity system.

Q: Will all 3 logo directions be shown as brand identities?
A: Yes. The three selected directions are developed into distinct and fresh visual identity directions so that you can compare different possibilities for your business.

Q: Are your logo designs minimalist?
A: Our approach focuses on creating designs that are fresh, clean, and minimalistic while still having a meaningful conceptual connection with the business.

Q: Why do you prefer minimal logo design?
A: Minimal design can help create a clearer, more recognizable, and more versatile identity. The objective is not simply to make a logo simple, but to remove unnecessary elements while retaining the core idea.

Q: Do you follow current logo design trends?
A: We focus on creating fresh and relevant identities rather than simply following trends. The design direction is developed around the business and its long-term identity.

Q: What happens after the logo and typography are developed?
A: We create relevant mockups and prepare a professional design presentation to demonstrate how the identity can work in practical brand applications.

Q: Why do you create mockups for a logo?
A: Mockups help demonstrate how the proposed identity can look in real-world applications and make it easier to understand the overall visual impact of the design.

Q: How do you present the logo concepts to the client?
A: We prepare a professional design presentation showing the developed directions, their visual treatment, relevant versions, typography, identity elements, and mockups.

Q: Will I see the logo in real-world applications?
A: Yes. We create mockups as part of the presentation so you can see how the identity translates into practical applications.

Q: Can I choose between the 3 logo directions?
A: Yes. The three developed directions are presented so you can evaluate and select the direction you feel is most appropriate for your business.

Q: What makes your logo design process different from simply creating a logo?
A: We do not begin by randomly creating symbols on a computer. We first understand the business through a detailed briefing, explore concepts through mind mapping, develop ideas through sketching, digitally refine the strongest directions, work on typography and identity, and finally present the concepts through professional mockups.

Q: Do you use ready-made logo templates?
A: No. Our process begins with business-specific research through the briefing, conceptual mind mapping, and original sketch development rather than selecting and modifying a ready-made logo template.

Q: Do you use Canva templates for your logo designs?
A: No. The logo concepts are developed through our own conceptual and design process rather than using Canva templates.

Q: Do you simply generate logos using AI?
A: No. AI-generated logo outputs are not the basis of our logo design process. We develop concepts through briefing, mind mapping, sketching, design exploration, typography, and identity development.

Q: Can I give you references of logos I like?
A: Yes. Your references and preferences can be included in the briefing and help us understand your visual expectations. The final concepts are developed specifically for your business.

Q: Can I tell you which colours I like?
A: Yes. Colour preferences and choices are covered in the briefing and are considered during the identity development process.

Q: What if I don't know which colours are right for my business?
A: You can explain your preferences and expectations in the briefing. We use our design understanding along with the business context to develop an appropriate visual direction.

Q: What if I don't know what style of logo I want?
A: That is completely fine. The briefing is designed to help us understand your preferences even if you cannot define a specific logo style. The creative exploration is then developed based on your business and requirements.

Q: Can you create a logo that is both unique and simple?
A: Yes. Our process specifically explores unique conceptual ideas and develops them into fresh, clean, and minimalistic identity directions.

Q: Can you make a logo based on my business name?
A: Yes. The business name and the nature of the business are considered as part of the creative exploration. Depending on the brief, the logo can explore typographic, symbolic, conceptual, or combined directions.

Q: Can you create a logo using a symbol related to my business?
A: Yes. During mind mapping, we specifically explore words and concepts that can be visually represented while remaining connected to the business subject.

Q: Can you combine multiple ideas into one logo?
A: Yes. During the conceptual exploration, one, two, or even three relevant directions or ideas can be combined when doing so creates a stronger and more meaningful visual concept.

Q: What if I want a logo that doesn't use an obvious industry symbol?
A: Our mind-mapping process allows us to explore less obvious words and concepts connected to your business, which can lead to more distinctive visual ideas rather than relying only on obvious industry symbols.

Q: Why don't you show hundreds of logo options?
A: Our approach focuses on developing strong, considered directions rather than overwhelming the client with a large number of random options. We explore extensively during the conceptual stage and present the strongest 3 directions.

Q: Why do I get only 3 logo concepts?
A: The objective is quality rather than quantity. We explore many ideas internally through mind mapping and sketching, then select the strongest 3 directions for professional development and presentation.

Q: Can I get more than 3 concepts?
A: The standard logo design package is structured around 3 developed creative directions. Any requirement outside the agreed scope would need to be discussed separately.

Q: How many revisions are included?
A: The logo design package includes 2 rounds of revisions.

Q: What happens after I select one of the concepts?
A: The selected direction can be refined through the included revision process, after which the final identity is prepared according to the agreed scope.

Q: Can you change the logo after I select a direction?
A: Yes. The package includes 2 rounds of revisions for refining the selected direction based on your feedback.

Q: Can I change the entire concept during revisions?
A: Revisions are intended to refine the selected direction. A completely new conceptual direction after approval of a concept may fall outside the standard revision scope.

Q: Why do you show mockups instead of just sending the logo file?
A: A logo needs to be evaluated as part of a brand identity, not only as an isolated graphic. Mockups help demonstrate how the identity behaves in practical applications.

Q: What will I see in the final logo presentation?
A: The presentation shows the developed logo directions, colour versions, black-and-white versions, line-drawing versions, typography, identity treatment, and relevant mockups.

Q: Is this service just logo design or branding?
A: The process goes beyond creating a standalone logo. It includes developing the logo, typography, colour treatment, visual identity, and presentation of the identity through mockups.

Q: Can you design a logo for a new startup?
A: Yes. The detailed briefing and strategic creative process are particularly useful for understanding a new business and developing an identity aligned with its direction.

Q: Can you redesign an existing logo?
A: Yes. We can understand your existing identity through the briefing and develop new creative directions based on your current brand and future requirements.

Q: Can you create a logo for an established business that wants a fresh identity?
A: Yes. We can explore fresh and minimalistic directions while considering the existing business, its positioning, and future plans.

Q: Why should I choose a professional logo design instead of an online logo maker?
A: An online logo maker generally gives you automated or template-based options. Our process involves understanding your business in depth, developing concepts specifically for it, exploring ideas through mind mapping and sketching, and creating a complete visual identity around the selected direction.

Q: Is the ₹20,000 fee only for drawing a logo?
A: No. The fee covers the complete creative process-from the detailed briefing and conceptual exploration to sketching, development of 3 directions, typography, identity development, mockups, and professional presentation.

Q: What makes your logo design worth ₹20,000?
A: The value lies in the depth of the creative process. We invest time in understanding your business, exploring meaningful concepts, developing multiple directions, refining the strongest ideas, and building the selected visual direction into a professional identity rather than simply producing a graphic.

Q: Can I get a logo for ₹5,000 or ₹10,000 instead?
A: Our standard logo design package is ₹20,000 + GST. The package is designed around our complete professional logo and identity development process.

Q: Is GST included in the logo design price?
A: No. The logo design fee is ₹20,000 plus GST.

Q: Can you guarantee that my logo will be trademarked?
A: We can create an original custom identity with trademark considerations in mind, but trademark registration or legal approval cannot be guaranteed through the design service.

Q: Will my logo look like other logos in my industry?
A: Our process is specifically designed to explore original concepts connected to your business rather than simply copying common industry symbols. The goal is to create a fresh and distinctive identity.

Q: Do you copy logos from Pinterest or other brands?
A: No. References can help us understand your preferences, but the actual logo is developed through our own conceptual process based on your business.

Q: Can you make my logo look exactly like a logo I found online?
A: We can understand what you like about the reference and use it to understand your preferences, but we do not simply copy another company's logo. The final direction is developed specifically for your business.

Q: Do you guarantee that nobody else has a similar logo?
A: We focus on creating original design work, but no designer can guarantee worldwide uniqueness across every existing logo without a formal trademark and legal search.

Q: How long does the complete logo design process take?
A: The exact timeline depends on the project scope, feedback, and approval stages. A specific delivery timeline should be confirmed when the project is scheduled.

Q: Do you provide the logo in different formats?
A: Final file formats and deliverables depend on the agreed project scope. The required formats should be confirmed as part of the project.

Q: Do I receive the editable source file?
A: Source-file delivery depends on the agreed project scope and should be confirmed before finalizing the project.

Q: Can I use the final logo on my website and social media?
A: The final identity is designed to be practical for business use. Specific usage rights and final deliverables depend on the agreed project scope.

Q: Can I use the logo for printing?
A: Yes, the identity is developed with practical brand applications in mind. The appropriate final artwork formats can be provided according to the agreed deliverables.

Q: Can you design a logo that works at both large and small sizes?
A: Yes. The design process considers the fundamental visual form of the logo and includes different versions such as colour, black-and-white, and line-drawing treatments to support versatile use.

Q: What is the main goal of your logo design process?
A: The goal is to create a fresh, minimalistic, meaningful, and distinctive identity that is connected to the business and can represent it professionally over the long term.